//! PyO3 hashmaps over the Cartesian product of common scalar dtypes.
//!
//! 9 key dtypes (`bool`, `i8`, `i16`, `i32`, `i64`, `u8`, `u16`, `u32`,
//! `u64`) × 11 value dtypes (the same 9 plus `f32` + `f64`) = 99 PyO3
//! classes, all generated by `hashmap_macro::define_hashmap!` (see
//! `hashmap_macro.rs`). Class names follow the pattern
//! `HashMap<K><V>` with each component spelled in PascalCase
//! (`HashMapU32U16`, `HashMapI64F64`, `HashMapBoolBool`, …).
//!
//! ## Surface
//!
//! Every class exposes the same API (documented on the macro):
//!
//! - `__new__(capacity: int = 0)` — preallocate buckets when
//!   `capacity > 0`; zero-arg form preserved for back-compat.
//! - `get(key) / lookup(key) -> Optional[V]`
//! - `set(key, v) / insert(key, v)`
//! - `lookup_ndarray(keys)` — vectorized lookup; misses become the
//!   per-dtype sentinel (table below).
//! - `insert_ndarray(keys, values)` — batch insert, last-wins on dup
//!   keys.
//! - `clean()` — clear entries, retain capacity (`HashMap::clear`).
//! - `__len__()`, `__contains__(key)`.
//!
//! ## Miss sentinel per value dtype
//!
//! | Value dtype     | Sentinel                                |
//! |-----------------|-----------------------------------------|
//! | `bool`          | `false`                                 |
//! | `i8`/`i16`/`i32`/`i64` | `<dtype>::MIN`                   |
//! | `u8`/`u16`/`u32`/`u64` | `<dtype>::MAX` (all-ones)        |
//! | `f32`/`f64`     | quiet NaN (`f32::NAN` / `f64::NAN`)     |
//!
//! Callers should check membership with `__contains__` / `lookup` when
//! the sentinel value is itself a legitimate entry value.

mod carrier_signs;
mod flat_segments;
mod hashmap_macro;
mod identity_gather;
mod inline_bytes;
mod number_idx_2d;
